WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
The overhead matrix connects software actions to
hardware work.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.584
First count resource quantities, then multiply by
service time with consistent units.

00:00:09.584 --> 00:00:15.866
Summing provides a simple baseline, while the
resource vector supports later contention analysis.

00:00:15.866 --> 00:00:22.212
Two designs with the same baseline time can behave
differently under load if they concentrate work

00:00:22.212 --> 00:00:23.572
on different devices.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.296
The ATM workshop turns graph reduction into a
complete baseline estimate.

00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:32.350
Combine validation, a selected transaction and
result delivery.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:38.333
State the branch-probability mapping rather than
silently inferring it from extracted labels.

00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:44.509
The resulting average is conditional on that mapping
and omits contention, so use it as input to

00:00:44.509 --> 00:00:48.369
further analysis rather than a production latency
guarantee.
